"""Build substantive industry and service-area children of the group-training hub."""
from __future__ import annotations
import json
from html import escape
from pathlib import Path

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]; OUT=ROOT/'docs'/'group-training'; BASE='https://www.910cpr.com'
INDUSTRIES={
'restaurants':('CPR and First Aid Training for Restaurants and Waitstaff','restaurants and food-service teams','Adult CPR and AED, choking response, burns, cuts, falls, sudden illness, and bleeding control are practical priorities. Bloodborne Pathogens awareness may be relevant where occupational exposure can occur.','waitstaff, kitchen staff, supervisors, and managers','First Aid/CPR/AED is usually a better starting point than BLS for ordinary restaurant roles. Training can be planned before opening or around shifts.','workplace',['hospitality','workplaces']),
'churches':('CPR Training for Churches and Ministry Teams','churches, ministries, and faith organizations','Cardiac arrest, choking, injuries, and emergencies involving children can occur during services, nursery care, and large events. AED readiness and a coordinated response matter.','ushers, security teams, childcare volunteers, clergy, and ministry leaders','Choose adult-only, adult-and-pediatric, or broader emergency readiness based on programs and attendees. Volunteers can practice the same response plan even when experience levels differ.','community',['childcare','community-organizations']),
'dental-offices':('BLS and Bloodborne Pathogens Training for Dental Offices','dental practices','Clinical teams may face medical emergencies and occupational exposure. BLS, AED and bag-mask skills where appropriate, Bloodborne Pathogens, and practice-specific scenarios can be coordinated.','dentists, hygienists, assistants, and front-office personnel','Clinical staff often need BLS, while front-office staff may need First Aid/CPR/AED. A mixed-role program avoids placing every employee into BLS automatically.','healthcare',['medical-offices','workplaces']),
'medical-offices':('BLS Training for Medical Offices and Clinics','medical offices and outpatient clinics','Cardiac, respiratory, pediatric, bleeding, and exposure events vary by specialty. BLS commonly supports clinical personnel; ACLS or PALS may fit only supported roles.','clinical personnel, practice managers, and front-office responders','Coordinate different credentials, Bloodborne Pathogens, bleeding control, expiration tracking, and renewal planning without treating all roles as equivalent.','healthcare',['dental-offices','workplaces']),
'schools':('CPR and First Aid Training for Schools','schools and education teams','Schools should plan for cardiac arrest, asthma or sudden illness, playground injuries, choking, and age-specific emergencies.','teachers, coaches, nurses, administrators, transportation, and support staff','Pediatric content may be relevant, but the school or district requirement controls the certifying body and course. Training can be staged around calendars and staff groups.','childcare',['childcare','fitness']),
'childcare':('Pediatric First Aid and CPR for Childcare Centers','childcare centers and early education programs','Pediatric breathing, cardiac, choking, allergic, illness, and injury emergencies require age-appropriate practice and a coordinated facility response.','teachers, directors, float staff, and other caregivers','Pediatric First Aid/CPR/AED is a common starting point, subject to exact licensing and employer wording. Confirm the card and agency named in that requirement.','childcare',['schools','churches']),
'workplaces':('CPR and AED Training for Offices and Workplaces','offices, worksites, and employee response teams','Sudden cardiac arrest, falls, bleeding, burns, and acute illness are foreseeable across many workplaces. AED placement and an internal response plan support the trained team.','designated responders, supervisors, safety staff, and interested employees','An OSHA-accepted First Aid/CPR/AED program is commonly appropriate, subject to the employer’s exact requirement. BLS is not the default for general employees.','workplace',['construction','fitness']),
'hospitality':('CPR, Choking, and Bleeding Control for Hospitality Teams','hotels, venues, and hospitality teams','Guest cardiac arrest, choking, falls, cuts, bleeding, and sudden illness call for calm coordination across public spaces.','front desk, food service, security, supervisors, and event staff','Build from First Aid/CPR/AED, then add choking, bleeding-control, and property-specific scenarios as supplemental practice.','workplace',['restaurants','churches']),
'fitness':('CPR and Emergency Training for Gyms and Fitness Staff','gyms, studios, coaches, and fitness staff','Exertion-related cardiac arrest, falls, heat illness, asthma, and injuries make AED readiness and practiced roles important.','trainers, instructors, coaches, desk staff, and managers','First Aid/CPR/AED often fits general fitness staff. Professional rescuers or employer-specified roles may require BLS.','fitness',['aquatics','workplaces']),
'aquatics':('CPR and BLS Training for Aquatics and Recreation Staff','aquatics and recreation programs','Drowning, respiratory emergencies, cardiac arrest, injuries, and pediatric events require rapid team coordination.','lifeguards, coaches, recreation staff, supervisors, and facility leaders','Professional rescuers may need BLS or an agency-specific credential. The employer’s written requirement controls; general recreation roles may follow a different course.','public_safety',['fitness','schools']),
'construction':('First Aid and CPR Training for Construction and Industrial Teams','construction and industrial teams','Falls, bleeding, crush or tool injuries, electrical events, burns, and sudden cardiac arrest are relevant to worksite planning.','designated responders, foremen, safety personnel, and crews','Start with workplace First Aid/CPR/AED and consider bleeding control and site-specific scenarios. Exact employer and contract requirements govern acceptance.','workplace',['workplaces','community-organizations']),
'community-organizations':('CPR and First Aid Training for Community Organizations','community organizations and nonprofit teams','Public events, volunteers, varied ages, cardiac arrest, choking, falls, and sudden illness call for a shared response plan.','staff, volunteers, program leaders, drivers, and event teams','First Aid/CPR/AED is a practical base. Add pediatric, choking, bleeding-control, or organization scenarios when the people served make them useful.','community',['churches','schools'])}
LOCATIONS={
'wilmington-nc':('Wilmington, North Carolina','New Hanover County','Wrightsville Beach, Carolina Beach, and nearby New Hanover County communities','healthcare and dental practices, schools, offices, hospitality teams, and community organizations','Wilmington is the core service market, but a complete address is still needed to validate instructor travel and the exact session window.'),
'jacksonville-nc':('Jacksonville, North Carolina','Onslow County','Camp Lejeune-area communities, Richlands, and nearby Onslow County','medical and dental offices, childcare programs, workplaces, fitness teams, and community groups','Jacksonville requests require address-based travel review from the instructor’s actual starting point; military or contract language must be supplied exactly.'),
'lumberton-nc':('Lumberton, North Carolina','Robeson County','Pembroke and reasonably reachable Robeson County communities','healthcare offices, industrial teams, schools, churches, and nonprofits','Lumberton service is scheduled case by case. Group size, course duration, instructor coverage, and travel economics can affect confirmation and pricing.'),
'whiteville-nc':('Whiteville, North Carolina','Columbus County','Lake Waccamaw and reasonably reachable Columbus County communities','workplaces, schools, churches, restaurants, and community organizations','Whiteville sessions may be held at the customer’s suitable facility after travel, room, equipment, and staffing are confirmed.'),
'myrtle-beach-sc':('Myrtle Beach, South Carolina','Horry County','Conway, North Myrtle Beach, and reasonably reachable Grand Strand communities','restaurants, hotels, attractions, fitness programs, medical offices, and workplaces','Myrtle Beach is a travel market. Potential dates require independent review for distance, course duration, group size, instructor coverage, and any travel charge.')}
GTM="""<script>(function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f)})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-PQS8DCBH');</script>"""
def page(slug,title,desc,h1,body,faq,kind,industry='',market='',related=''):
 url=f'{BASE}/group-training/{slug}/'; schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@graph':[{'@type':'Organization','@id':f'{BASE}/#organization','name':'910CPR / Coastal CPR Training','url':BASE},{'@type':'Service','name':h1,'provider':{'@id':f'{BASE}/#organization'},'url':url,'areaServed':market or ['North Carolina','South Carolina']},{'@type':'BreadcrumbList','itemListElement':[{'@type':'ListItem','position':1,'name':'Home','item':BASE+'/'},{'@type':'ListItem','position':2,'name':'Group training','item':BASE+'/group-training.html'},{'@type':'ListItem','position':3,'name':h1,'item':url}]}]}
 q=f'?industry={industry}&market={escape(market)}&source_page_type={kind}'
 return f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{escape(title)} | 910CPR</title><meta name="description" content="{escape(desc)}"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow"><link rel="canonical" href="{url}"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/group-training.css?v=20260906.1">{GTM}<script type="application/ld+json">{json.dumps(schema,separators=(',',':'))}</script></head><body><noscript><iframe src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=GTM-PQS8DCBH" height="0" width="0" style="display:none;visibility:hidden"></iframe></noscript><header class="top"><a class="brand" href="/index.html"><img src="/images/logo.png" alt=""><span>910CPR</span></a><a href="tel:+19103955193">910-395-5193</a></header><main><nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/group-training.html">Group training</a> / {escape(h1)}</nav><article class="authority"><p class="kicker">{escape(kind.replace('_',' '))}</p><h1>{escape(h1)}</h1><p class="lede">{escape(desc)}</p>{body}<h2>What 910CPR needs to schedule</h2><p>Provide the complete training address, participant estimate, employee roles, exact credential wording, delivery preference, operational constraints, and preferred dates. Candidate dates are not confirmed until travel, conflicts, instructor qualifications, duration, setup, cleanup, equipment, and staffing are reviewed.</p><h2>Delivery, equipment, and group planning</h2><p>Training can occur at a customer facility when the room, seating, floor or practice space, accessibility, equipment, and group size support the selected course. 910CPR supplies the agreed instruction and training equipment. The organization supplies an appropriate facility and coordinator. Initial, renewal, blended, and mixed-role needs can change duration and logistics.</p><h2>Certification and supplemental learning</h2><p>A certification card applies only to the completed certification course and certifying organization. Bloodborne Pathogens, Bleeding Control, choking-focused practice, and organization-specific scenarios may be separate modules. They do not automatically become one combined certification card. American Heart Association, American Red Cross, and Health &amp; Safety Institute credentials should not be treated as interchangeable when a requirement names one.</p><h2>Keep the team current</h2><p>After confirmation, the durable LanderWare session can support the later roster, attendance, card-record, expiration, and renewal workflow. Those lifecycle steps are coordinated separately from this initial request.</p><h2>Common questions</h2>{faq}<p><a class="primary" href="/group-training.html{q}">Configure and request this training</a></p>{related}</article></main><script>window.dataLayer=window.dataLayer||[];window.dataLayer.push({{event:'group_training_view',industry:{json.dumps(industry or 'unknown')},market:{json.dumps(market or 'unknown')},recommended_program:'unknown',selected_program:'unknown',reservation_mode:'requires_confirmation',source_page_type:{json.dumps(kind)}}});</script></body></html>'''
def build():
 OUT.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
 for slug,(h1,audience,risks,roles,fit,industry,links) in INDUSTRIES.items():
  body=f'<h2>Who this training is for</h2><p>This guidance is for {escape(audience)}. {escape(risks)}</p><h2>Who should be trained</h2><p>Consider {escape(roles)}. Train by actual role and written requirement, not job title alone.</p><h2>Which course is usually appropriate?</h2><p>{escape(fit)}</p><h2>Planning around operations</h2><p>Use shifts, staggered groups, or an agreed low-impact window. The right plan balances coverage with enough hands-on practice; it does not promise a universal duration or group limit before the course and headcount are known.</p>'
  faq='<h3>Can training occur at our facility?</h3><p>Yes, when the facility and requested date pass address, travel, room, equipment, and staffing review.</p><h3>How far ahead should we plan?</h3><p>Earlier requests provide more options. No standard lead time is promised because course, travel, instructor, and group requirements differ.</p><h3>How do we confirm the exact credential?</h3><p>Copy the employer, regulator, licensing, contract, or agency wording into the scheduler. 910CPR will match against that text before confirmation.</p>'
  rel='<h2>Related guidance</h2>'+''.join(f'<a href="/group-training/{x}/">{escape(INDUSTRIES[x][0])}</a><br>' for x in links)+'<p>See service guidance for <a href="/group-training/wilmington-nc/">Wilmington</a>, <a href="/group-training/jacksonville-nc/">Jacksonville</a>, <a href="/group-training/lumberton-nc/">Lumberton</a>, <a href="/group-training/whiteville-nc/">Whiteville</a>, and <a href="/group-training/myrtle-beach-sc/">Myrtle Beach</a>.</p>'
  d=f'Role-based on-site CPR, AED, First Aid, and related training guidance for {audience}, with a direct path to legitimate scheduling.'
  dest=OUT/slug/'index.html';dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);dest.write_text(page(slug,h1,d,h1,body,faq,'industry',industry,'',rel),encoding='utf-8')
 for slug,(market,county,nearby,orgs,truth) in LOCATIONS.items():
  h1=f'On-Site CPR Training in {market}';d=f'On-site CPR, First Aid, AED, BLS, and group-training guidance for organizations in {market} and reasonably served nearby communities.'
  body=f'<h2>On-site service in {escape(market)}</h2><p>910CPR provides on-site training by confirmed request for {escape(orgs)}. {escape(truth)}</p><h2>Communities reasonably served</h2><p>Requests may be considered in {escape(nearby)}. This page does not claim a permanent classroom, office, local instructor, routine availability, or fixed response time in {escape(market)}.</p><h2>Course and program choices</h2><p>Programs may include BLS, First Aid/CPR/AED, pediatric First Aid/CPR/AED, ACLS, PALS, Bloodborne Pathogens, Bleeding Control, choking practice, and organization-specific scenarios when supported and appropriate.</p><h2>Travel, timing, and pricing</h2><p>Travel is evaluated from the assigned instructor’s actual starting location. Group size, duration, setup, cleanup, qualifications, existing sessions, personal blocks, operating hours, equipment, overnight needs, and trip economics can affect feasibility and price. The scheduler therefore labels market dates as requiring confirmation unless every rule has been validated.</p>'
  faq=f'<h3>Can we use our own facility in {escape(market)}?</h3><p>Yes, after the address, room, furniture, accessibility, and practice space are reviewed.</p><h3>Are the same dates offered in every city?</h3><p>No. A potential time for {escape(market)} must pass its own travel and instructor review.</p><h3>What organizations commonly request training here?</h3><p>{escape(orgs.capitalize())} may request programs matched to their roles and written requirements.</p>'
  rel='<h2>Industry guidance</h2><p><a href="/group-training/dental-offices/">Dental offices</a>, <a href="/group-training/restaurants/">restaurants</a>, <a href="/group-training/churches/">churches</a>, <a href="/group-training/childcare/">childcare</a>, and <a href="/group-training/workplaces/">workplaces</a>.</p>'
  dest=OUT/slug/'index.html';dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);dest.write_text(page(slug,h1,d,h1,body,faq,'location','',market,rel),encoding='utf-8')
if __name__=='__main__': build()
